<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Clemens returns one week after intake and is seen by Dr. Ifeanyi-Strand of geriatric psychiatry on the same day. The nurse called him three days after intake; he had used his safety plan once, calling a friend on a bad evening. He still thinks of his wife many times a day, keeps her room as it was, and avoids the photograph albums; he says that part of him died with her and that his work seems pointless. He sleeps four to five hours. He still has passing thoughts that he would like to join her, with no wish to act on them, and he has kept whisky to one glass. He has had no chest tightness this week, having walked slowly. He has cut to about ten cigars a day but is not ready to stop. His intake tests showed a high urate, LDL cholesterol 150 mg/dL, hemoglobin A1c 5.8 percent and normal thyroid and vitamin B12 levels; the ECG was normal. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Grief</td><td>Daily yearning and preoccupation; avoids reminders; PG-13-R 41</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Four to five hours</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Passing thoughts of joining his wife, no intent; safety plan used once</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>About ten cigars a day; not ready to stop</td></tr><tr><td>Intake results</td><td>Urate 8.6 mg/dL; LDL 150 mg/dL; hemoglobin A1c 5.8%; TSH and B12 normal; ECG normal</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

