  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Prolonged grief disorder (F43.81)</content>. Dr. Ifeanyi-Strand confirms prolonged grief disorder: more than a year after his wife&apos;s death, he has daily yearning and preoccupation with her and more than three of the accessory symptoms, and the grief exceeds what is expected in his community and culture and stops him working and seeing friends. Major depression is not present: his low mood is tied to the loss, his sense of worth is intact, his humor and interest return away from reminders, and he has fewer than five depressive symptoms. No antidepressant now. Safety reviewed: passive thoughts of death without intent; the safety plan stands. [S]<list><item>Prolonged grief disorder therapy, sixteen weekly sessions with the clinic psychologist, starting next week.</item><item>PG-13-R and PHQ-9 every four weeks.</item><item>Sleep plan: fixed rising time, no cigar or whisky late in the evening, no sleeping pill.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chest tightness on exertion (R07.89)</content>. No episodes this week; ECG normal. [S]<list><item>CT coronary angiography booked for the morning of the five-week visit.</item><item>Call 911 for chest pain at rest or lasting more than fifteen minutes.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Tobacco use disorder (F17.290)</content>. Cut from fifteen to about ten cigars a day; not ready to set a quit date. [S]<list><item>Revisit with the CT result.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Grief severity (PG-13-R) and the DSM-5-TR prolonged grief disorder criteria</td><td>At diagnosis and every four weeks during therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PG-13-R 41, above the threshold of 30; DSM-5-TR criteria met (confirmed by geriatric psychiatry)</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Prolonged grief disorder therapy: sessions attended</td><td>Weekly for sixteen weeks</td><td>Ordered</td><td>First session booked for next week</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression (PHQ-9), to watch for major depression</td><td>At baseline and every four weeks during treatment</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 11 at intake (item 9 scored 1); major depression not present on interview; repeat at five weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk review, safety plan, means safety and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Passive thoughts of joining his wife without intent or plan; no firearms; whisky kept to one glass; safety plan used once; 988 in his phone</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep, without sedative-hypnotics</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Four to five hours; sleep plan given; no sedative-hypnotic, as the Beers criteria advise</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Social contact and his writing</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Has seen one friend this week; not writing</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco use (cigars a day), readiness and counseling</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About ten cigars a day; not ready to quit; advice linked to his heart</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Chest symptoms on exertion</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None this week; resting ECG normal at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT coronary angiography for stable exertional chest tightness</td><td>Once, at evaluation</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Booked for the morning of the five-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>138/82 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Serum urate during allopurinol titration</td><td>Every 2 to 5 weeks while titrating, then every 6 months</td><td>Up to date</td><td>8.6 mg/dL at intake; allopurinol to be discussed once the chest pain evaluation is done</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Geriatric psychiatry consultation</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen by Dr. Ifeanyi-Strand today</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>PG-13-R below 30 and back to writing and seeing friends. In progress; target 2026-10-16 [S]</item><item>No thoughts of death and a safety plan he would use. In progress; target 2026-09-11 [S]</item><item>Stop smoking cigars. In progress; target 2026-10-16 [S]</item><item>LDL cholesterol at least 50 percent lower on a high-intensity statin. In progress; target 2026-09-11 [S]</item><item>Serum urate below 6 mg/dL and no gout flares. In progress; target 2026-10-16 [S]</item><item>Six or more hours of sleep on most nights without a sleeping pill. In progress; target 2026-10-16 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Prolonged Grief Disorder (DSM-5-TR criteria, patient and family information) (2022); Validation of the new DSM-5-TR criteria for prolonged grief disorder and the PG-13-Revised (PG-13-R) scale (2021); Treatment of complicated grief: a randomized controlled trial (2005); Optimizing Treatment of Complicated Grief: A Randomized Clinical Trial (2016); Loss of partner and suicide risks among oldest old: a population-based register study (2004); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); 2021 AHA/ACC/ASE/CHEST/SAEM/SCCT/SCMR Guideline for the Evaluation and Diagnosis of Chest Pain (2021); 2020 American College of Rheumatology Guideline for the Management of Gout (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, ischemic heart disease, hyperlipidemia, and depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Grief therapy weekly from next week. Five-week review with the CT coronary angiogram that morning. Call the clinic or 988 at any time. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-17: five-week review: CT coronary angiography result, a statin and aspirin, a plan to quit smoking, and starting allopurinol. [S]</paragraph></text>

